<%#
  The add/remove control itself, with no wrapper of its own so the caller decides
  what turbo replaces. One control rather than two, because a digital file is
  either in the cart or it is not - there is no quantity to nudge, so a second
  press should undo the first.

  Both mutating branches are real forms, not links: they change state, and a GET
  that mutates gets fired by every link prefetcher going.

  Routed through Buttons::Component rather than hand-rolled classes. That is what
  supplies the pill radius the system reserves for actions, a border token that
  clears 3:1, the focus ring, and - via aria_label - a name that distinguishes
  this card's button from the eleven identical ones beside it.

  locals: product, size (:sm on a shop card, :lg on the product page)
%>
<% size = local_assigns.fetch(:size, :sm) %>
<%# py-4 on both: the grid button was ~36px, under the 44px thumb target this
    site's primary user needs one-handed in the dark %>
<%# w-full on the grid: the card stacks price over button, so the button
    fills the card rather than sitting beside a price it cannot fit next to %>
<% shape = size == :lg ? "py-4 px-6.5" : "py-4 px-5 w-full" %>

<% if current_user&.awaiting_payment?(product) %>
  <%# Paid for, and Paddle has not confirmed it yet. This branch is the whole
      point: without it the button read "Dodaj do koszyka" for something the
      buyer had just been charged for, and pressing it charged them again.

      Not a button - there is nothing to press and nothing to undo - but not a
      dead end either: it goes to the row in the account where the wait is
      explained, and where it will turn into a player on its own.

      Neutral rather than amber. The One Lamp Rule gives the light to the action
      worth taking, and waiting is not one. %>
  <% label = content_block("shop.card.awaiting") %>
  <%= render Buttons::Component.new(
    text: label,
    href: dashboard_index_path(anchor: dom_id(product)),
    pill: true,
    variant: :outline,
    icon: icon("clock", class: "size-4 shrink-0"),
    aria_label: "#{label} - #{product.name}",
    classes: "hover:cursor-pointer text-t6! font-bold! border-border-input! text-tan! hover:text-cream! #{shape}"
  ) %>
<% elsif current_user&.purchased?(product) %>
  <%# bought already, and a digital file is bought once - so this leads to where
      it actually is rather than offering to sell it again. The server refuses the
      add too; this is the half the buyer can see. %>
  <% label = content_block("shop.card.owned") %>
  <%# href is anchored to the row: the label promises "listen in your account",
      and landing at the top of a library with no highlight left the buyer to
      find it themselves - worst at the moment they have just paid %>
  <%= render Buttons::Component.new(
    text: label,
    href: dashboard_index_path(anchor: dom_id(product)),
    pill: true,
    variant: :outline,
    aria_label: "#{label} - #{product.name}",
    classes: "hover:cursor-pointer text-t6! font-bold! border-accent! text-accent! hover:bg-accent! hover:text-ink! #{shape}"
  ) %>
<% elsif current_cart.include?(product) %>
  <% label = content_block("shop.card.remove") %>
  <%= button_to cart_item_path(product_id: product.id), method: :delete,
        form_class: "contents",
        aria: { label: "#{label} - #{product.name}" },
        data: { turbo_submits_with: t("forms.removing") },
        class: "inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-1.5 whitespace-nowrap rounded-full border border-border-input bg-ink text-cream font-bold text-t6 cursor-pointer transition-all duration-100 ease-in-out select-none hover:bg-ink-soft focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-accent #{shape}" do %>
    <%= label %>
  <% end %>
<% else %>
  <% label = content_block("shop.card.add") %>
  <%= form_with url: cart_items_path, class: "contents" do |form| %>
    <%= form.hidden_field :product_id, value: product.id %>
    <%# turbo_submits_with: the tap used to produce nothing until the stream
        landed, so on bad signal it read as a miss and invited a second tap -
        which, by then, removed the item %>
    <%= form.button type: :submit,
          aria: { label: "#{label} - #{product.name}" },
          data: { turbo_submits_with: t("forms.adding") },
          class: "inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-1.5 whitespace-nowrap rounded-full border border-accent-terracotta/30 bg-accent text-ink font-bold text-t6 cursor-pointer transition-all duration-100 ease-in-out select-none hover:bg-accent-hover focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-accent #{shape}" do %>
      <%= label %>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
<% end %>
